.TH MAINUAN-WELCOME 1 "October 2026" "mainuan-welcome 2.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mainuan-welcome \- Mainuan welcome and first-login assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mainuan-welcome
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mainuan-welcome
opens the Mainuan Welcome window. It lets the user choose the visual style,
theme, accent colour and desktop layout, and installs media codecs, the
antivirus, the firewall, office suites and web browsers.
.PP
Starting a second copy brings the open window to the front.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/org.mainuan.Welcome.desktop
System-wide entry that opens the Welcome at login.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/org.mainuan.Welcome.desktop
Written with
.B Hidden=true
when the user unticks "Mostrar esta tela ao iniciar o sistema".
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/mainuan-welcome/mainuan-welcome-helper
Privileged helper run through
.BR pkexec (1);
it accepts only fixed installation profiles.
.TP
.I /var/log/mainuan-welcome/install.log
Output of the last package installation (readable by root).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR flatpak (1)
